       "before": "default",
       "after": "default"
      }
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "type": "accordion",
      "header": "",
      "items": [
       {
        "title": "Autofocus for »pilot«",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>With the help of the CNC control of the spindle (C axis), the tool cutting edges are automatically moved and sharpened, even with multi-edged cutting tools. This guarantees user-independent measurement results.</p>",
          "images": [
           {
            "src": "/fileadmin/_processed_/6/4/csm_csm_SK_50_high_precision_spindle-ZOLLER_e70d471b61_c389a775c3.webp",
            "alt": "",
            "w": 290,
            "h": 162
           }
          ],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "below",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "textpic",
          "id": "c2226",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Precise/exact angle measurement",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>The rotation sensor positions the C axis fully automatically to the target angle. This enables high-precision measurement of spiral angles and pitches as well as wobble compensation.</p>",
          "images": [
           {
            "src": "/fileadmin/_processed_/a/d/csm_csm_Vericut_measured_tool-screenshot-ZOLLER_357ae1d600_4a86f55306.webp",
            "alt": "",
            "w": 290,
            "h": 163
           }
          ],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "below",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "textpic",
          "id": "c3280",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Manual fine setting",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>Hand wheels facilitate fine adjustment of the X-axis and Z-axis, especially for tool inspection.</p>",
          "images": [
           {
            "src": "/fileadmin/_processed_/b/b/csm_csm_smile_420_fine_adjustment-ZOLLER_fd50d7b925_d8302e2c8d.webp",
            "alt": "",
            "w": 288,
            "h": 161
           }
          ],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "below",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "textpic",
          "id": "c3282",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Center height measuring device",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>A perfectly set center height increases tool life and thus reduces your tool costs. At the same time, you shorten setup times, avoid scrap, and improve the quality of your workpieces.</p>",
          "images": [
           {
            "src": "/fileadmin/_processed_/9/9/csm_csm_smile_optic_carrier_center_height_measuring_system-ZOLLER_c344e3ae11_9276a06dce.webp",
            "alt": "",
            "w": 290,
            "h": 162
           }
          ],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "below",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "textpic",
          "id": "c3284",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Tool inspection",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>For axial and radial inspection and testing of the contours of radii, angles, distances, and wear and tear in incident light, with 50x magnification of the tool cutting edge.</p>",
          "images": [
           {
            "src": "/fileadmin/_processed_/2/2/csm_csm_smile_venturion_450_tool_inspection-ZOLLER_3f128a74b5_ef3f06365c.webp",
            "alt": "",
            "w": 290,
            "h": 193
           }
          ],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "below",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "textpic",
          "id": "c3286",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "»zidCode« with labels",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>With »zidCode«, data is printed quickly and simply onto labels and can be scanned directly at the machine. This means error-free data transfer.</p>",
          "images": [
           {
            "src": "/fileadmin/_processed_/9/d/csm_csm_zidCode-Datentransfer-Scanner-ZOLLER_19b3ed04a4_f5a458a4de.webp",
            "alt": "",
            "w": 290,
            "h": 162
           }
          ],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "below",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "textpic",
          "id": "c3288",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Manual tool identification",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>The write/read head is manually moved to the RFID chip on the tool holder. The chip can then be read and written to.</p>",
          "images": [
           {
            "src": "/fileadmin/_processed_/9/d/csm_csm_smile_tool_identification_hand-ZOLLER_d004fe28de_406c13087a.webp",
            "alt": "",
            "w": 290,
            "h": 162
           }
          ],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "below",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "textpic",
          "id": "c3290",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Semi-automatic tool identification",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>The read/write unit is manually moved in the Z direction to the height of the RFID chip on the tool holder. The movement of the write/read head in the X-axis is CNC-controlled. When the read/write unit hits the RFID chip, it can be read and written to.</p>",
          "images": [
           {
            "src": "/fileadmin/_processed_/b/b/csm_csm_smile_tool_identification_hand_and_cnc-ZOLLER_87a4f6f0dd_2170b2f144.webp",
            "alt": "",
            "w": 290,
            "h": 162
           }
          ],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "below",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "textpic",
          "id": "c3292",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       }
      ],
      "ftype": "accordion",
      "id": "c2228",
      "bg": "",
      "space": {
       "before": "default",
       "after": "default"
      }
     }
    ]
   ],
